 {"id": "README-005", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P4", "title": "P4 \u2014 README Install block downloads a 404: it pins the unreleased tag v0.1.11 (both /releases/download/v0.1.11/ URLs return 404, checksum verify fails, the 'binary' is the HTML error page)", "reasoning": "Doc severity P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) \u2014 that is policy, not a new assessment of this defect.\n\nTHE DEFECT: the Install block a stranger runs first downloads nothing. README.md:17 states the current release is v0.1.11 and README.md:20-23 hands over two /releases/download/v0.1.11/ URLs; no v0.1.11 tag or release exists. Local tags top out at v0.1.10; curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/coding-hermes/boardctl/releases/latest | jq -r .tag_name -> v0.1.10; curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -L https://github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/releases/download/v0.1.11/SHA256SUMS -> 404 (the same probe against v0.1.10 -> 200).\n\nEXACT COMMANDS AND OUTPUT (clean scratch dir, 2026-10-17, HEAD 625a30f):\n  curl -sL -o boardctl_linux_amd64 https://github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/releases/download/v0.1.11/boardctl_linux_amd64   -> rc=0 (curl does not fail on a 404; it writes the error page)\n  curl -sL -o SHA256SUMS https://github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/releases/download/v0.1.11/SHA256SUMS                       -> rc=0\n  head -3 SHA256SUMS                       -> \"Not Found\"\n  sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS -> \"sha256sum: SHA256SUMS: no properly formatted checksum lines found\"  (rc=1)\n  chmod +x boardctl_linux_amd64; ./boardctl_linux_amd64 version -> \"./boardctl_linux_amd64: line 1: Not: command not found\"  (rc=127)\nSame four lines with v0.1.10 substituted: \"boardctl_linux_amd64: OK\" (rc=0) and \"boardctl version v0.1.10\" (rc=0). The block is correct \u2014 only the tag it names is unreal.\n\nTHE SAME FILE CONTRADICTS ITSELF: README.md:35-37 and README.md:77,81 repeat the v0.1.11 identity claim, while README.md:962 and README.md:1003-1006 say the post-v0.1.10 flags are NOT in the published v0.1.10 binary, and README.md:1248-1263 probes v0.1.10 as the release. The Go path silently disagrees too: go install github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/cmd/boardctl@latest installs v0.1.10 and prints \"boardctl version v0.1.10\" (rc=0), so a reader who takes README.md:50-54 gets an older binary than README.md:17 claims is current.\n\nWHY CI DOES NOT CATCH IT: make version-check exits 0 at HEAD both with and without VERSION_TAG=v0.1.11 (README.md:1289-1293 documents that the gate checks agreement between README surfaces, not the currency of the tag). Green gate, 404 download.\n\nFIX (either) + ACCEPTANCE:\n  (a) revert to the newest real release: README.md:17 -> v0.1.10 and every /releases/download/<tag>/ URL -> v0.1.10, keeping the existing since-v0.1.11 annotations \u2014 this also clears the reader-visible symptom of pending DF-BOARDCTL-39 and of blocked DOC-26; or\n  (b) cut v0.1.11 (candidates RELEASE-2026-10-01-01 / RELEASE-2026-10-04-01 are blocked pending owner release authorization) and then re-run README.md:19-24 verbatim on the published asset.\nDone when: on a clean machine the four lines of README.md:19-24 run as written \u2014 sha256sum -c exits 0 and ./boardctl_linux_amd64 version prints the tag named in README.md:17.\n\nNOT A FINDING HERE: \"Current release\" drift is not a wording problem; the fix is a pin change or a release, and a doc worker can do (a) alone.\n\nRELATED ROWS: DF-BOARDCTL-39 (pending; same release-ahead class, for the normalize-board verb), DOC-26 (blocked), RELEASE-2026-10-01-01 / RELEASE-2026-10-04-01 (blocked), README-001 (closed; earlier version-string drift).", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs", "readme"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T14:00:53.691194+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-18T09:50:00-05:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "9b1cee1be69bf046f95bd9f4be1fda3ed5498f7c5554c898fc1f5fe90609d5c5"}, "foreman_note": "Premise stale: v0.1.11 release was cut after this row was filed (2026-10-17). Verified live 2026-10-18: gh release view v0.1.11 -> isDraft=false, tagName=v0.1.11; curl SHA256SUMS -> HTTP 200. Commit ad951c3 already moved README pins to v0.1.11. Closing as premise-stale, no code change needed.", "worker_status": "complete"}
