 {"id": "README-008", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P5", "title": "P5 \u2014 the Development block omits 'make spec-check' (a gate ci.yml runs), and the repo-layout table describes ci.yml as 'build, vet, test' only", "reasoning": "Doc severity P5 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (coverage/polish; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) \u2014 policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: the Development block omits a gate CI actually runs, so a contributor cannot reproduce the CI gate set from the README \u2014 and a gate that lands without a README line stays invisible.\n\n.github/workflows/ci.yml steps, in order: Build (go build ./...), Vet (go vet ./...), Gofmt (go test -count=1 -run TestGofmt ./internal/fmtcheck), Version-check (internal/versioncheck), Spec-check (go test -count=1 ./internal/speccheck), Install govulncheck v1.7.0, Vulnerability-check (internal/vulncheck), Test (go test -short -count=1 ./...).\n\nREADME.md:1153-1160 lists: go build ./cmd/boardctl, go test ./..., make fmt-check, make version-check, make vuln-check, make release. grep -n 'spec-check' README.md -> no match. make spec-check (Makefile:78; runs go test -count=1 ./internal/speccheck) was executed in this sweep -> \"ok github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/internal/speccheck\" (rc=0), so the target is real, green, and unmentioned.\nREADME.md:1127 describes the same workflow as \"CI (build, vet, test)\", under-describing its gate set.\n\nFIX: add a `make spec-check` line to the Development block (README.md:1153-1160) with the one-line purpose \u2014 the serve/OpenAPI parity gate CI enforces (docs/muster/openapi.yaml vs the serve wiring) \u2014 and update the ci.yml row at README.md:1127 to name the real steps.\nACCEPTANCE: every gate ci.yml runs is runnable from the Development block, and README.md:1127's description matches ci.yml's steps.\n\nVERIFIED THIS SWEEP (so the row does not overstate): make fmt-check rc=0, make version-check rc=0, make vuln-check rc=0 (govulncheck pin already installed), make spec-check rc=0, go test ./... all packages ok.\nRELATED ROWS: none open; README-005/006/007 filed the same tick.", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs", "readme"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T14:00:53.757742+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T14:00:53.815161+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "eb647979931678aefe88e32441c92989359d0dadafa7c4800d5f26a59013f2de"}, "foreman_note": "README-health lane tick boardctl-readme-2026-10-17-13-47-37 (session filed 2026-10-17). Two-way coverage finding: the README never names a command the release binary carries. Probe log: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/boardctl/probe-20261017.log"}
 {"id": "README-009", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P5", "title": "P5 \u2014 README.md:1216 states the go.mod toolchain pin as \"go 1.26.6\"; go.mod:3 declares \"go 1.26.9\" (BT-080 bumped the directive 2026-10-09 and left the README sentence stale)", "reasoning": "Doc severity P5 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) \u2014 that is policy, not a new assessment of this defect. Class: accuracy (a documented value that contradicts the file the README names as its source).\n\nTHE DEFECT\nREADME.md:1216-1219 (section \"Deployment freshness gate (BT-057)\") states the repo's toolchain pin and names the file that carries it, and the value it names is no longer in that file:\n\n  README.md:1216  \"The toolchain requirement: go.mod declares `go 1.26.6`. The Go 1.26.5 standard library shipped reachable advisories that 1.26.6 fixes \u2014 `net/http` (GO-2026-6089), `crypto/tls` (GO-2026-6090) and `encoding/asn1` (GO-2026-5972) \u2014 so a lower `go` directive, or a build with an older toolchain, fails this gate.\"\n\nEXACT COMMANDS AND OUTPUT (2026-10-17, HEAD 94e5b56, which is origin/main; probe log /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/boardctl/probe-go-version-20261017.log)\n  grep -n '1\\.26' README.md\n    -> 1216:The toolchain requirement: go.mod declares `go 1.26.6`. ...\n  sed -n '3p' go.mod\n    -> go 1.26.9\n  git log --format='%ad %h %s' --date=short -L 3,3:go.mod\n    -> 2026-10-09 3c83aa8 fix(vuln): bump go 1.26.6 -> 1.26.9 \u2014 7 reachable stdlib vulns (net/http, crypto/tls, net/textproto, mime/multipart)\n    -> 2026-09-17 08655c4 fix: pin the toolchain to go 1.26.6 and add the dependency-vulnerability gate. Addresses BT-033.\n\nCAUSE (both rows complete, so nothing is pending on the code side)\nThe paragraph was written for BT-033 (2026-09-18, commit 08655c4), when `go 1.26.6` really was the pin. BT-080 (P1, complete 2026-10-09, commit 3c83aa8) bumped the directive to 1.26.9 and left README.md:1216 alone. The sentence is now false in two ways: the value it names, and the advisory list behind it (the 1.26.9 bump cleared GO-2026-6603/6607/6608/6611/6612/6613/6617 \u2014 7 advisories \u2014 not the 3 named here).\n\nWHY NO GATE CATCHES IT\ninternal/versioncheck is the repo's README gate, but it compares only README release-tag surfaces (`Current release: **vX.Y.Z**` and every /releases/download/<tag>/ URL); it never reads the `go` directive, and there is no `make docs-check`/`docs-drift` target. Verified: `grep -rn '1\\.26' internal/versioncheck/` -> no match; `grep -n 'docs-check' Makefile` -> no match; `make version-check` -> \"ok github.com/coding-hermes/boardctl/internal/versioncheck\" (rc=0). So README-vs-go.mod drift is structurally unguarded while the gate is green.\n\nIMPACT\nA contributor who reads \"the requirement is 1.26.6\" and builds with GOTOOLCHAIN=local on a 1.26.6 toolchain meets the directive-mismatch the same paragraph tells them to respect; with the default GOTOOLCHAIN=auto the 1.26.9 toolchain is fetched silently, so the sentence misstates why their build behaves as it does.\n\nFIX (one line)\nREADME.md:1216 -> \"go.mod declares `go 1.26.9`\", and restate the following sentence for the current pin (the 1.26.9 bump cleared the 1.26.6-and-earlier reachable advisories). Keep the closing instruction (\"Do not lower the directive to silence the gate; raise it to the patched release instead\") unchanged.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n`grep -n '1\\.26' README.md` shows the value on README.md:1216 equal to the value on line 3 of go.mod, and the paragraph's advisory sentence no longer asserts a superseded patch level.\n\nUNVERIFIED\nThe GOTOOLCHAIN=local refusal on an actual 1.26.6 toolchain was NOT reproduced on this box (that toolchain is not installed); that sentence is read from README.md:1220-1222's own text, not measured here.\n\nRELATED ROWS\nBT-080 (complete \u2014 the bump that orphaned the sentence), BT-033 (complete \u2014 the bump the sentence was written for). No open README row covers this value; README-005..008 (filed by this lane earlier in the same tick) cover the release pin, two refusing examples, the install-check table and the Development-block gate list.\n\nch:trace row=README-009 spec=README.md#deployment-freshness-gate-bt-057 wave=none:serial-tick test=none:no-test-covers-readme-vs-go.mod doc=README.md prompt=~/.hermes/skills/coding-hermes/coding-hermes-readme/SKILL.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/boardctl/probe-go-version-20261017.log witness=path@origin:go.mod verdict=none:no-judge commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:tick-local", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs", "readme"], "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-10-17T14:07:15.260944+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T14:07:15.289131+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "9f5d32fedd07d5694a9bb9f9da5414db16c4079d00a7d708649fb60eccb4ce24"}, "foreman_note": "README-health lane tick boardctl-readme-2026-10-17-13-47-37 (session filed 2026-10-17). Cross-refs: BT-080 (complete, commit 3c83aa8 \u2014 the bump that orphaned the sentence), BT-033 (complete, commit 08655c4 \u2014 the bump the sentence was written for). No open row covers this value; the lane's earlier findings this tick are README-005..008. Probe log: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/readme/boardctl/probe-go-version-20261017.log"}
