 {"id": "DOC-34", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "title": "P4 \u2014 document `update --replace`: `--note` APPENDS by default, `--replace` OVERWRITES foreman_note (the only overwrite path, in no repo doc)", "reasoning": "Doc severity P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (missing reference; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) -- policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: `boardctl update --replace` is registered - cmd/boardctl/main.go:816, `replace := fs.Bool(\"replace\", false, \"with --note: overwrite foreman_note instead of appending\")` - and is listed in the subcommand's own usage text (cmd/boardctl/main.go:858, \"[--replace]\"); the --note registration itself already documents the pair at cmd/boardctl/main.go:811 (\"foreman_note (appends to the existing note; --replace overwrites)\") with the BT-68 rationale at :812, but it appears in NO repository doc: README.md has zero hits, docs/ has zero hits, skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md has zero hits. README's update block documents `--note` (README.md:106-112) without ever saying that the default is APPEND, and therefore never introduces the only flag that overwrites. A reader concludes notes are append-only and cannot erase a wrong note.\n\nEVIDENCE (T3; scratch board /tmp/bt-docs-scratch2, target repo untouched - the exact commands are in the artifact):\n  $ boardctl -C $S update SCR-0 --note \"note A\"       -> updated task SCR-0: foreman_note, updated_at\n  $ boardctl -C $S update SCR-0 --note \"note B\"       -> foreman_note = \"note A\\n\\nnote B\"        (APPEND, default)\n  $ boardctl -C $S update SCR-1 --note \"only note\" --replace -> foreman_note = \"only note\"        (OVERWRITE)\n  $ grep -c -- '--replace' README.md docs/** skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md  ->  0\nArtifact: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md\n\nARTIFACT TO WRITE: README.md, the update usage block (README.md:98-116) plus the \"Worktree, branch and session fields\" neighbourhood if a note paragraph lives there.\nREADER: operator / foreman - the flag is the only way to correct a row note.\nACCEPT: README states that `--note` APPENDS by default and that `--note X --replace` OVERWRITES `foreman_note`; both statements reproduce against a scratch board with the two-output diff above quoted in the row's close-out.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-34 spec=none:audit-lane-finding test=none:doc-gap doc=README.md#usage evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md witness=none:no-external-surface verdict=none:audit-lane commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:audit-lane task=document update --replace overwrite semantics", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.434281+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.434281+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ee3f79d8979532569482e2f5f5eaa60e25477b6b56052904485ed8e50aaf52b1"}, "foreman_note": null}
