 {"id": "DOC-38", "type": null, "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "title": "P4 \u2014 document `create --complexity` and `--depends-on` in the README create examples", "reasoning": "Doc severity P4 by Bane's 2026-09-30 ruling (missing reference; doc findings are P4/P5, never P1-P3) -- policy, not a new assessment.\n\nTHE DEFECT: `create` registers `--complexity` (cmd/boardctl/main.go:658, \"complexity (default 3)\") and `--depends-on` (cmd/boardctl/main.go:659, \"comma-separated dependency ids\"), and its own usage text lists both (cmd/boardctl/main.go:690). The README create examples document --priority, --reasoning, --capability-tags, --evidence-run-id, --worktree, --branch and --session (README.md:84-97) - every sibling flag except these two. `grep -c -- '--complexity' README.md` = 0 and `grep -c -- '--depends-on' README.md` = 0; README discusses the depends_on FIELD at length (README.md:187, 699-722) without ever naming the flag that writes it. --depends-on is the higher-value half: it is the write-side entry to the dangling-dependency gate (`validate --fail-on dangling-dep`, README.md:417, and the gate rejects an id that does not exist yet - docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md:100), so an integrator can write a dependency only by reading `--help`.\n\nEVIDENCE (T3; scratch board /tmp/bt-docs-scratch2, target repo untouched):\n  $ boardctl -C $S create --id SCR-1 --title \"child\" --complexity 2 --depends-on SCR-0\n  created task SCR-1 (appended to .../tasks.jsonl)\n  $ grep -o '\"complexity\":[0-9]*\\|\"depends_on\":\\[[^]]*\\]' .../tasks.jsonl   (SCR-1 row)\n  \"complexity\":2   \"depends_on\":[\"SCR-0\"]\n  $ grep -c -- '--complexity' README.md   ->  0\n  $ grep -c -- '--depends-on' README.md   ->  0\nArtifact: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md\n\nARTIFACT TO WRITE: README.md, the create examples (README.md:84-97).\nREADER: integrator / foreman authoring rows (dependency edges are the board's link graph).\nACCEPT: README's create block shows `--complexity N` and `--depends-on A,B`; the depends-on line names the existence check (an unknown id is refused at write time) and the resulting `depends_on` array; the documented invocation reproduces the row fields quoted above.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-38 spec=none:audit-lane-finding test=none:doc-gap doc=README.md#usage evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/boardctl/2026-10-17-surface-diff.md witness=none:no-external-surface verdict=none:audit-lane commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=none:audit-lane task=document create --complexity/--depends-on", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["docs"], "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.532537+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-17T19:32:55.532537+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c6c4d1f78725cd11ff396e0bcdeb76f78b7aa4479ad117eee969fde987d008dc"}, "foreman_note": null}
-{"id": "DF-BOARDCTL-43", "type": null, "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "title": "P2 REPO-HYGIENE: this repo tracks .coding-hermes/board/board.db, so its own doctor FAILs (git-tracked-set error) \u2014 and TestDoctorRepoBoardNoTrackedCaches skips .db files, so the tracked case is ungated", "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-10-19 (foreman tick boardctl-foreman-2026-10-19-04-45-20, while closing README-006).\n\nEVIDENCE (all live, on a clean checkout at f6d54e6):\n  $ ./bin/boardctl doctor -C .\n  [error] git-tracked-set: .coding-hermes/board/board.db is tracked under .coding-hermes/board \u2014 JSONL-canonical boards must not track db/parquet caches\n  RESULT: FAIL (1 error(s), 10 warning(s))\n  $ git ls-files .coding-hermes/board/\n  .coding-hermes/board/board.db        <-- tracked\n  .coding-hermes/board/board.jsonl\n  .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl\n  .coding-hermes/board/fixtures.jsonl\n  .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl\n  $ git log --diff-filter=A --oneline -- .coding-hermes/board/board.db\n  37ab3b1 fix: errcheck \u2014 check fmt.Fprintf return in repair-events JSON path\n  => the 12KB board.db cache was ADDED by an unrelated errcheck commit; no commit ever intended to track it.\n  $ grep -n board .gitignore\n  8:.coding-hermes/board/.lock      <-- only the lock is ignored; board.db is NOT\n  $ ls -la .coding-hermes/board/board.db -> 12288 bytes, mtime 2026-10-12 05:43\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: the repo whose contract is JSONL-canonical boards (and whose doctor exists to police exactly this: df-boardctl-35 made tracked caches an ERROR and untracked fossils a warning) fails its own gate. docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md:288 already states the rule (\"The board files are git-tracked \u2014 NEVER commit a board.db/*.parquet\"); the live repo breaks it. Any consumer that reads doctor status as green is misreading a FAIL.\n\nTHE UNGATED HALF (why no test caught it): internal/board/doctor_test.go:266 TestDoctorRepoBoardNoTrackedCaches deliberately SKIPS .db/.parquet entries when copying the live board into a fresh git repo (lines 282-284: \"the live board dir may carry an UNTRACKED cache\"). That skip was written for the untracked-fossil case, and it also masks the TRACKED case \u2014 so a committed board.db is invisible to the suite while doctor errors in production. A test that consults the REAL tracked set (e.g. `git ls-files .coding-hermes/board` from the module root and assert no .db/.parquet) closes the blind spot; TestDoctorGitTrackedDBError (line 305) already proves the detector itself works on a synthetic board.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (2 files + 1 test):\n  1. `git rm --cached .coding-hermes/board/board.db` (keep the local file; it is a retired cache \u2014 doctor calls such fossils \"safe-to-remove caches\").\n  2. .gitignore: ignore .coding-hermes/board/*.db and *.parquet (belt-and-braces vs. a future `git add -A`).\n  3. Replace/extend TestDoctorRepoBoardNoTrackedCaches with an assertion over the live git-tracked set so the tracked case can never regress silently.\nACCEPTANCE: `./bin/boardctl doctor -C .` on a fresh clone reports 0 errors (the board.db line becomes a warning or disappears); `git ls-files .coding-hermes/board/` lists only the four JSONL files; the new test FAILS on a repo that tracks a board.db (RED-proven) and passes at HEAD.\n\nRELATED: DF-BOARDCTL-35 (complete \u2014 built the tracked-error/untracked-warning split), docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md:288, skills/boardctl-usage/SKILL.md:420 (never `git add -A` a board copy).", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["go", "ci", "hygiene"], "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-19T05:08:30.004575+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-19T07:32:57.955856+00:00", "detail": {"fingerprint": "aaf4133768acc0f7b7adb2507bfe71898387a1674792a562ecfe99c8096b8075", "evidence": [{"run_id":"0087689b","ts":"2026-10-19T07:32:57.955856+00:00"}]}, "foreman_note": "Worker delivered. Test asserts the real tracked set via git ls-files, fails on any .db/.parquet. board.db moved from tracked ERROR to untracked WARNING. Full suite green.", "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "1a890b2", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "board.db untracked + .gitignore *.db/*.parquet + TestDoctorRepoBoardNoTrackedCaches rewritten to assert git ls-files (RED-proven). doctor -C . exits 0 with 0 errors. Judge PASS 0087689b."}
